{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfukgNJKskEHQ1GhmKmnH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As far as I know, Workflows has no per-workflow setting to cap concurrency. The only limit is the account-wide concurrent-instance limit, and instances created beyond it wait in a `queued` state until a slot frees up. The exact numbers change, so check the current Workflows limits page.\n\nTo set your own cap, put a throttle in front of instance creation:\n\n- **Queues:** Have producers send a message per job, and have a consumer Worker call `env.MY_WORKFLOW.create()`. Set `max_concurrency` on the consumer. This limits how fast instances start, but not how many are running, unless the consumer waits for each instance to finish.\n- **Durable Object semaphore:** Keep a counter in a Durable Object. Acquire a slot before `create()`, and release it when the workflow finishes, either from a final workflow step or after polling `instance.status()`. This enforces a true cap on running instances.\n\nMy knowledge may be out of date, so check the Cloudflare Workflows docs in case a native concurrency option has since been added."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2253,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2253},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44259673-a201-4c58-9a70-9299b23e514d","uuid":"82501285-17bf-455b-8789-d4949bd8d5a8","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:39:12.348Z","request_id":"req_011CfukgN4SrUCADkJCzNrZG"}
